course: dictionary
lesson: 15749
title: Trespassing: going where you are not allowed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Trespassing means going onto someone's land or into a building without permission. Permission means being allowed. If nobody has said you may go there, you are trespassing.
explain: «The farmer put up a sign: No Trespassing.» The sign tells you the field belongs to someone and you must stay out. Clues like sign, private, permission and danger all point to the meaning of trespassing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Ella was trespassing in the farmer's field» means Ella went into the field without permission. It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Trespassing means going onto someone's land or into a building without permission.
fact: Trespass is the verb: «Do not trespass on the railway.» Trespassing is the action, and it is often used with on: «trespassing on the farm.»
fact: «No Trespassing» and «Private Property» signs are often found on farms, railways and building sites.
fact: These places can be dangerous, so trespassing there is not safe.
fact: «Trespassers will be prosecuted» means people who go onto land without permission may be taken to court.
exercise: «The sign said No Trespassing, so Sam stayed on the path.» What does No Trespassing tell Sam? | It is a school trip | Come in and have a look | *Do not go onto this land without permission | The land is for sale
exercise: «Ella climbed over the fence into the farmer's field without asking.» What is Ella doing? | *Trespassing | Looking for the bus stop | Helping the farmer | Visiting her cousin
exercise: Which word means going onto someone's land without permission? | shopping | playing | *trespassing | picnicking
test: «The railway sign said Keep Out, so Maya went home.» Why is the sign important? | It shows where the station is | *It warns that trespassing on the railway can be dangerous | It says the trains are late | It is a picnic area
test: What does «Trespassers will be prosecuted» tell you? | Everyone is welcome to come in | Trespassers get a prize | *People who go onto land without permission may be taken to court | The land is for sale
exam: Which sentence shows trespassing? | Walking your dog in the public park | Buying bread at the corner shop | *Going into the locked factory without permission | Reading a book in the library
